{"step_index":495,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:27:43Z","thinking":"**Formulating Z3 for Rad+1 > Roman Dom.**\n\nConsidering a Z3 script is needed to test the conjecture `rad(G) + 1 > romanDominationNumber(G)`.  The goal is to determine if *any* graph exists that satisfies this inequality. The plan is to check for graphs up to a certain size, say n=20, and see if Z3 reports UNSAT or a counterexample.\n\n\n**Simplifying Roman Domination Constraint.**\n\nEncoding Roman domination directly involves a universal quantifier which is challenging in the tool. The inequality `rad(G) + 1 > γR(G)` can be expressed existentially, avoiding the universal quantifier.  A graph's eccentricity must be greater or equal to W, and there must exist a Roman dominating function of weight W, which will satisfy the inequality. This simplifies the Z3 encoding significantly.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\\nfrom z3 import *\\nimport sys\\n\\ndef search_counterexample(n, W):\\n    s = Solver()\\n    # Adjacency\\n    adj = [[Bool(f\\\"adj_{i}_{j}\\\") for j in range(n)] for i in range(n)]\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        s.add(Not(adj[i][i]))\\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\\n            s.add(adj[i][j] == adj[j][i])\\n    \\n    # Distance bounds: d[i][j] in {0, ..., W}\\n    # d[i][j] <= k iff exists path of length <= k\\n    # Instead of full distances, let reach[k][i][j] be True if dist(i, j) <= k\\n    reach = [[[Bool(f\\\"r_{k}_{i}_{j}\\\") for j in range(n)] for i in range(n)] for k in range(W+1)]\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        for j in range(n):\\n            if i == j:\\n                s.add(reach[0][i][j])\\n            else:\\n                s.add(Not(reach[0][i][j]))\\n    \\n    for k in range(W):\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            for j in range(n):\\n                # reach[k+1][i][j] == reach[k][i][j] or exists m (reach[k][i][m] and adj[m][j])\\n                step = Or([And(reach[k][i][m], adj[m][j]) for m in range(n)])\\n                s.add(reach[k+1][i][j] == Or(reach[k][i][j], step))\\n    \\n    # Condition 1: rad(G) >= W\\n    # For every vertex i, there exists j such that dist(i, j) >= W (i.e. Not(reach[W-1][i][j]))\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        s.add(Or([Not(reach[W-1][i][j]) for j in range(n)]))\\n    \\n    # Condition 2: G is connected (HasRadius)\\n    # reach[n][i][j] is True for all i, j. For small n, reach[n-1] is full.\\n    # We can check connectivity at the end or enforce reach[n-1]\\n    \\n    # Condition 3: Exists Roman dominating function f with weight <= W\\n    # f[i] in {0, 1, 2}\\n    f = [Int(f\\\"f_{i}\\\") for i in range(n)]\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        s.add(Or(f[i] == 0, f[i] == 1, f[i] == 2))\\n        # if f[i] == 0, exists j with adj[i][j] and f[j] == 2\\n        dom = Or([And(adj[i][j], f[j] == 2) for j in range(n)])\\n        s.add(Implies(f[i] == 0, dom))\\n    \\n    s.add(Sum(f) <= W)\\n    \\n    res = s.check()\\n    if re\n<truncated 594 bytes>","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Running Z3 check on small graphs\"","toolSummary":"\"Run Z3 search for counterexample\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
